WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.395 --> 00:00:04.545
Unit seventeen. Vaccines and Public Health!

2
00:00:05.503 --> 00:00:10.106
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Sokha, your school doctor.

3
00:00:10.156 --> 00:00:13.209
Hi, Doctor Sokha! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.259 --> 00:00:17.752
Today we learn about Vaccines and Public Health. Let's go!

5
00:00:18.745 --> 00:00:22.745
Vaccine. Say it with me. Vaccine!

6
00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:30.092
Public health. Say it with me. Public health!

7
00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:38.083
Herd immunity. Say it with me. Herd immunity!

8
00:00:41.556 --> 00:00:46.156
Eradication. Say it with me. Eradication!

9
00:00:49.636 --> 00:00:53.569
Polio. Say it with me. Polio!

10
00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:00.871
Measles. Say it with me. Measles!

11
00:01:04.376 --> 00:01:08.910
Misinformation. Say it with me. Misinformation!

12
00:01:12.396 --> 00:01:15.896
Trust. Say it with me. Trust!

13
00:01:19.407 --> 00:01:32.484
Vaccines are among the greatest public health successes. Smallpox was eradicated, and polio is close. Misinformation can lower trust and allow measles to return, so herd immunity matters.

14
00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:35.894
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Sokha!

15
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.285
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.829
Herd immunity!

17
00:01:44.748 --> 00:01:49.981
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:50.031 --> 00:01:51.439
Misinformation!

19
00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:58.529
Did you know? Smallpox was officially declared eradicated in 1980!

20
00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:01.344
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:02:02.152 --> 00:02:11.034
Think and answer. How can misinformation affect vaccination rates?

22
00:02:11.084 --> 00:02:12.255
Great answer!

23
00:02:13.289 --> 00:02:18.635
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:18.685 --> 00:02:21.506
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

